# Downloading the ERA5 data

## Source

ERA5 hourly data on single levels from 1940 to present. Variable: **2 m temperature** (`2m_temperature`).  
DOI: https://doi.org/10.24381/cds.adbb2d47

## Steps

1. Create a free account at https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu
2. Accept the ERA5 terms of use
3. For each city, download the hourly time series using the
   [CDS time series tool](https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu/datasets/reanalysis-era5-single-levels-timeseries?tab=download)

**City coordinates used in this study:**

| City        | Latitude | Longitude |
|-------------|----------|-----------|
| Mexico City | 19.43    | −99.13    |
| Guadalajara | 20.67    | −103.35   |
| Monterrey   | 25.67    | −100.31   |
| Chihuahua   | 28.63    | −106.07   |
| Phoenix     | 33.45    | −112.07   |

4. Select: Product type → Time series; Variable → 2 m temperature;
   Period → as required; Format → NetCDF or CSV
5. Convert daily maximum from hourly values and save as `.xlsx`
   with a column named `i_tmax`
